# linux-desktop/files/fcitx5-wayland/environment
#
# System-wide environment for a native Wayland desktop running Fcitx5.
# Deploy to:
#   /etc/environment
#
# Read this file before assuming it is right for the machine you are on.
#
# VERIFICATION (2026-11-22): the reasoning under GTK_IM_MODULE / QT_IM_MODULE
# below was NOT the cause of the browser failure. The cause was that Fcitx5
# was not KWin's input method; with Fcitx 5 selected as the Plasma virtual
# keyboard, Chrome and Firefox typed with or without the two variables. This
# file records what was deployed, not a recommendation -- see
# linux-desktop/wayland-fcitx5-rime.md, root cause 4.
#
# ONE variable, on purpose:
#
#   XMODIFIERS=@im=fcitx
#     Points X11 and XWayland clients at Fcitx5's XIM server. The server name
#     is `fcitx`, NOT `fcitx5` -- Fcitx5 registers its XIM under the older
#     name for compatibility, and `fcitx5-diagnose` will say
#     `Environment variable XMODIFIERS is "@im=fcitx5" instead of "@im=fcitx"`
#     if it is wrong.
#
#     Note that the `fcitx5-autostart` package ships
#     `/etc/profile.d/fcitx5.sh`, which exports `XMODIFIERS=@im=fcitx` plus
#     `GTK_IM_MODULE` and `QT_IM_MODULE` for every GUI login. Do not edit that
#     packaged file (an upgrade overwrites it) and do not add the two toolkit
#     variables here:
#
#   GTK_IM_MODULE / QT_IM_MODULE
#     Deliberately ABSENT. On Wayland these tell the toolkit to use
#     Fcitx5's X11-era module instead of the Wayland input-method protocol,
#     which breaks native Wayland clients (Chrome, Firefox) while X11 and
#     D-Bus clients (Konsole, Dolphin, the Plasma search bar) keep working.
#     Fcitx5 says so at startup:
#       "Detect GTK_IM_MODULE and QT_IM_MODULE being set and Wayland Input
#        method frontend is working. It is recommended to use Wayland input
#        method frontend."
#
#     They still arrive in the session, because /etc/profile.d/fcitx5.sh runs
#     for every login. To see what a fresh login would actually inherit:
#
#       env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH=/usr/bin:/bin XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland \
#         bash -c 'for f in /etc/profile.d/*.sh; do [ -r "$f" ] && . "$f"; done;
#                    echo "GTK_IM_MODULE=[$GTK_IM_MODULE] QT_IM_MODULE=[$QT_IM_MODULE] XMODIFIERS=[$XMODIFIERS]"'
#
# See linux-desktop/wayland-fcitx5-rime.md for the full write-up.

XMODIFIERS=@im=fcitx
